**Quark Confinement**

Although the quark model describes the vast experimental results for thousands of hadrons, all attempts of isolating a single free quark have failed. The quarks are confined therefore can exist only as color neutral objects i.e. baryons or mesons. Apparently the color force does not drop off with distance like the other forces. It is postulated that it may actually increase with distance at the rate about 1 GeV/fm. A free quark is not observed because by the time the separascale, the energy is far above the pair production energy for quark-anti-quark pairs. One kind of the visualization of the confinement is called the "bag model". Quarks are contained in an elastic bag which allows them to move freely around within the bag. However as long as you try to pull a quark out, the bag stretches and resists.

